    "summary": "createBookings() validates room/owner/start/length, refuses overlapping bookings per room, lists a room's bookings by start, and lets only the owner cancel. Unit tests with Vitest against the real module and its memoryStore prove each rule and its refusal, including a concurrent double-booking check (the clash check and the add are separate awaits).",
    "inScope": [
      "book() validation and BookingError messages",
      "overlap rules incl. concurrent booking",
      "list() order and room filtering",
      "cancel() ownership and freeing time"
    ],
    "outOfScope": [
      "the app's database-backed BookingStore (not in the repo)"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Tests use the real createBookings with the default memoryStore; nothing is faked.",
      "Messages are asserted exactly as src/bookings.ts writes them, since only the message says why a booking was refused."
    ],
    "openQuestions": [
      "Should two simultaneous overlapping requests for the same room both be refused except one? The ticket implies yes; the code checks then adds across an await."
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Race: two concurrent overlapping bookings both succeed because the clash check and add are separate async steps",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "TC10 books concurrently and expects exactly one success"
      },
      {
        "description": "Off-by-one at boundaries (30/240 minutes, back-to-back)",
        "impact": "medium",
        "mitigation": "TC5, TC6, TC9"
      }
    ],
    "acceptanceCriteria": [
